{
  "about": [
    "The cleanup rules, written down once as examples that the Mac app and the Windows app must both pass.",
    "Each case runs the full cleanup on `in` and must produce exactly `out`. `config` holds only the cleanup.json keys that differ from the shipped defaults; it is read with the same loader as a real cleanup.json, so missing keys take their defaults.",
    "Each timed case banks its `segments` in order, the way the recognizer hands them over: the gap is the segment's `start` minus the previous segment's `end` (no gap is measured when either is missing, and a segment with no times keeps the previous end). The banked text then runs through the full cleanup and must produce `out`.",
    "Later steps add cases. Changing an existing case's `out` needs a changes.md entry, because it changes what users get."
  ],
